      "description": "Watch St. Truiden vs Omonia Nicosia highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The UEFA Europa League returned with high stakes on August 20, 2026, as St. Truiden hosted Omonia Nicosia in a match where patience and discipline were tested until the final whistle. Both sides looked to establish their dominance early on, setting the stage for a tense European encounter. A Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Period The match began with both St. Truiden and Omonia Nicosia showing great defensive organization. Throughout the first half, neither side was willing to commit too many men forward, leading to a disciplined battle in the midfield. Frederic Soelle Soelle looked for openings for the home side, but the Omonia Nicosia backline remained firm. As the referee blew for halftime, the score remained level, reflecting a balanced opening 45 minutes where clear-cut chances were hard to come by. Second Half Adjustments and Mounting Tension The second half saw an immediate change as Samed Bazdar replaced Frederic Soelle Soelle for the hosts. The intensity began to rise, and with it, the referee's involvement. Robert-Jan Vanwesemael was the first to see yellow in the 50th minute, followed closely by Jean-Kevin Duverne of Omonia Nicosia . Both managers looked to their benches to break the deadlock; Ryotaro Araki and Arbnor Muja were introduced for the home side, while the visitors brought on Anastasios Chatzigiovanis and later Loic Nego . Despite the fresh legs, the game remained locked in a physical struggle, highlighted by a late booking for Ewandro . Stoppage Time Drama at the Death Just as the match seemed destined for a goalless draw, the home crowd was sent into a frenzy. In the 4th minute of stoppage time, Ryan Merlen found space and delivered a precise pass to Shogo Taniguchi . The defender made no mistake, firing the ball home to break the deadlock at the last possible moment. The goal proved to be the final action of significance, as St. Truiden secured all three points in dramatic fashion right before the final whistle blew, leaving Omonia Nicosia with no time to respond."
